<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonardo Loredan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1436">1436</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lunardo Loredan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonardo Loredan was a Venetian nobleman and statesman who reigned as the 75th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doge-of-venice">Doge of Venice</a> from 1501 until his death in 1521. Born into the noble Loredan family, he traded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> before rising through the Republic's magistracies, among them Savio del Consiglio, podestà of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, ducal councillor and, from 1492, Procurator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-the-evangelist">Saint Mark</a>, one of the highest offices of the state. As doge he led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a>, in which the Republic was defeated in 1509 before a new alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> in 1513. Under his rule, in 1516, a decree isolated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of Venice in the first Ghetto.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonardo-loredan.jpg" alt="Leonardo Loredan" width="330" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Bellini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Bellini,_portrait_of_Doge_Leonardo_Loredan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Leonardo Loredan was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> on 16 November 1436, the eldest son of Gerolamo Loredan. After a classical education he traded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> to raise the family's finances; legend has it that a fortune-teller in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> foretold that he would be a prince in his homeland. In 1461 he married into the wealthy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giustiniani-family">Giustiniani family</a> and had nine children. Some historians hold that his later election owed as much to that family's influence as to his talent.</p><p>His public career began on 13 December 1455, at nineteen, as a lawyer in the Giudici di Petizion. He was Camerlengo di Comun in 1473 and Savio di Terraferma in 1481, and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> from 1487 to 1489. In July 1492 he became Procurator of Saint Mark. After Doge Agostino Barbarigo died on 20 September 1501, Loredan came first in the election that ended on 2 October, helped by the sudden death of his most popular rival, Filippo Tron.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">In office</h2><p>Loredan took office during the Second Ottoman–Venetian War, in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> had lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methoni">Modon</a> in 1500 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durazzo</a> in August 1501. With the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-gritti">Andrea Gritti</a>, he made peace in 1502–1503 at the price of territory and an annual tribute. A dispute with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> over papal lands Venice had occupied led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-cambrai">League of Cambrai</a>, formed in December 1508 by Maximilian I, Louis XII, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon">Ferdinand II of Aragon</a> and the pope.</p><p>After the defeat at Agnadello in 1509 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> fell, but Loredan called for sacrifice and total mobilisation, and it was retaken. By the treaty of Blois of 23 March 1513 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> allied with Louis XII, regained its lost territories and ended the war; under the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> of December 1516 Maximilian surrendered Verona. In 1516 a decree confined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of Venice to the first Ghetto. In his last years financial scandals multiplied and offices were bought at high prices.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Loredan fell ill in June 1521, developed gangrene in a leg and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> on 22 June 1521. He was buried in the church of Santi Giovanni e Paolo. A magistracy, the Inquisitors of the Dead, later fined his heirs 9,500 ducats. About 1572 a monument was raised to him there, with a statue by Girolamo Campagna and architecture by Girolamo Grappiglia. Giovanni Bellini's portrait of him, now in the National Gallery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, is one of the first frontal portraits of a reigning doge. Pompeo Batoni chose him in 1737 to represent the office of doge in The Triumph of Venice.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Leonardo Loredan” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.44,12.33&amp;year=1491" aria-label="Venice on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Leonardo Loredan"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5734 6163h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5734 6163h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.44,12.33&amp;year=1491">What was here in 1491? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
